  RELEVANCE: Companion piece to Cohen's same-issue reply ("Functional
  Explanation: Reply to Elster"); together they open the direct Cohen-Elster
  exchange around which this domain is organized.

  POSITION: Opening methodological-individualist salvo against Cohen's
  functionalism.
  },
  keywords = {functional-explanation, methodological-individualism, elster-cohen-exchange, High, INCOMPLETE, no-abstract}
}

@article{cohen1980functional,
  author = {Cohen, G. A.},
  title = {Functional Explanation: Reply to Elster},
  journal = {Political Studies},
  year = {1980},
  volume = {28},
  number = {1},
  pages = {129--135},
  doi = {10.1111/j.1467-9248.1980.tb01240.x},
  note = {
  CORE ARGUMENT: Responds directly to Elster's review, defending the
  legitimacy of functional explanation in historical materialism against the
  charge that it is inherently teleological or scientifically illegitimate
